-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",44,{
[1377]="700375D5\n1\tTalk to the fletcher\tThe fletcher is in Edoras. Hutha asked you to seek out the fletcher and learn if he has any arrows to spare.\n2\tCollect arrows (total: 3)\tThe arrows the fletcher mentioned are on the ground near him. You should collect the arrows the fletcher mentioned.\n3\tBring the arrows you collected to Hutha\tHutha is in Edoras. You should bring the arrows you received from the fletcher to Hutha.\n",
[1378]="7006B753\n1\tTalk to Tínsha\tMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. The fletcher, Tínsha, can be found at the east end of the crafters' wharf.\n2\tFind the smithy\tMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. Tínsha has requested that you bring her a crate of arrowheads from Gurtum, the arrowsmith. The smithy can be found at the north end of the crafters' wharf.\n3\tTalk to Gurtum\tMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. The fletcher has requested that you bring her a crate of arrowheads from the arrowsmith.\n4\tCarry the crate of arrowheads to Tínsha\tMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. The arrowsmith, Gurtum, has given you leave to take a crate of arrowheads to the fletcher, Tínsha.\n5\tTalk to Tínsha\tMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. Gurtum, the arrowsmith, has given you leave to take a crate of arrowheads to the fletcher. Tínsha. Tínsha is at the east end of the crafters' wharf.\n6\tBring the arrows to Dalagín\tMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. The fletcher has given you leave to take the tub of arrows to the Dumûri captain, Dalagín. Dalagín is near the archers' towers on the west side of Iridír.\n7\tTalk to Dalagín\tMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. The fletcher has provided a tub of arrows that you brought to Dalagín. You should talk to her.\n",
[1379]="7002EE5B\n1\tFind an Elf in the East Wall to ask about the arrow you discovered\tYou need to find an Elf somewhere in the East Wall who can study the arrow of Elf-make and tell you where it may have come from.\n",
[1380]="7001CCD3\n1\tCollect spent arrows (total: 10)\tSpent Malledhrim arrows may be found around the ruins of Fállug, west of Amon Angened. Thindiel has asked you to recover spent Malledhrim arrows from the ruins of Fállug.\n2\tBring spent arrows to Thindiel atop Amon Angened\tThindiel is at the way-post atop Amon Angened, east of Fállug. You should bring the arrows you collected to Thindiel.\n",
[1381]="7000AE16\n1\tReturn the wood to Sergeant-at-Arms Gautr at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect kindling (total: 5)\tKindling can be found among the fallen logs, and other pieces of wood found throughout the Ettenmoors. You will find a greater concentration near the Grimwood lumber-yard within Hithlad. Sergeant-at-Arms Gautr sent you into the Ettenmoors in search of wooden shafts or kindling. He is making arrows to supply the Elves who will guard the front channel of Tol Ascarnen.\n",
[1382]="700006B7\n1\tTalk to Hartrím at the entrance of Garth Agarwen\tMake your way to the entrance to the area known as Garth Agarwen, north-east of the Eglan-camp, and speak with Hartrím. Dannasen asked you to seek out Hartrím at the entrance to Garth Agarwen in an effort to discover if he has found any of the shields once used by Dannasen and his brethren.\n2\tBring the shields of Arthedain to Hartrím\030Collect shields of Arthedain (total: 20)\tThe Hillmen of Rhudaur who serve the Red-maid and their brigand allies can be found in Garth Agarwen, the fortress of the Red-maid in the north-east of Agamaur. Hartrím awaits you outside the gates of Garth Agarwen. Dannasen, one of the shades of Arthedain cursed by Iarwain Ben-adar, fears that the others have lost their resolve to break their curse, believing that the Red-maid is too powerful. To strengthen their resolve, Dannasen enlisted Hartrím of the Eglain to collect the shields they lost to Rhudaur long years ago. Hartrím, too weak to face these foes, turns to you for assistance.\n",
[1383]="7000130A\n1\tCollect steam-scorched carapaces (total: 12)\030Collect Hogni's spiked helmet\tNerbyg can be found in the Eastern Malenhad in Angmar. Hogni Cleave-shank can be found at Gabilazan in the Misty Mountains. Dawn Stockard has asked you to bring her norbog-carapaces and Hogni Cleave-shank's spiked helmet.\n2\tBring first set of components to Dawn Stockard\tDawn Stockard is in the town of Archet, north of Bree. Dawn Stockard is waiting for you to return with the first set of components.\n3\tCollect corroded Neekerbreeker-horns (total: 20)\030Collect grisly bat-talons (total: 20)\tNerbyg can be found in the Eastern Malenhad in Angmar. Bats can be found in Angmar and other dangerous places. Dawn Stockard has asked you to bring her corroded Neekerbreeker-horns and grisly bat-talons.\n4\tBring second set of components to Dawn Stockard\030Collect corroded Neekerbreeker-horns (total: 20)\030Collect grisly bat-talons (total: 20)\tDawn Stockard is in the town of Archet, north of Bree. Dawn Stockard is waiting for you to return with the second set of components.\n5\tCollect Badge of Command\030Collect putrid slime of Helchgam\tHelchgam can be found beneath the evil city of Carn Dûm in Angmar. Lagmâs can be found at Urugarth in Angmar. Dawn Stockard has asked you to bring her the putrid slime of Helchgam and a Badge of Command.\n6\tBring last set of components to Dawn Stockard\030Collect Badge of Command\030Collect putrid slime of Helchgam\tDawn Stockard is in the town of Archet, north of Bree. Dawn Stockard is waiting for you to return with the last set of components she needs.\n",
[1384]="70000F26\n1\tCollect snowbeast-furs (total: 12)\030Collect Driftclaw's hide (quantity: see journal)\tSnow-beasts can be found in the north-western corner of the Misty Mountains near the Bruinen Source. Driftclaw can be found in the Misty Mountains, in the land of the giants, in the south-eastern corner. Sterling Proudfoot asked you to collect Driftclaw's wind-swept hide and snowbeast-furs.\n2\tBring first set of components to Sterling Proudfoot\tSterling Proudfoot is in Buckland, west of Bree and east of the Brandywine River. You should bring the hide and furs to Sterling Proudfoot.\n3\tCollect unyielding drake-scales (total: 20)\030Collect glossy cave-claw hides (total: 10)\tThe drakes and cave-claws which bear the required components can be found in Angmar and other dangerous places. Sterling Proudfoot asked you to bring him drake-scales and cave-claw hides to aid him in his task.\n4\tBring the second set of components to Sterling Proudfoot\030Collect unyielding drake-scales (total: 20)\030Collect glossy cave-claw hides (total: 10)\tSterling Proudfoot is in Buckland, west of Bree and east of the Brandywine River. You should bring the scales and hides you collected to Sterling Proudfoot.\n5\tCollect goblin-badge of rank\030Collect Insignia of Battle\tAkrúr can be found guarding the path to the great drake Lhugrien near Urugarth in Angmar. Sorkrank and Burzfîl can also be found in Urugarth. Sterling Proudfoot asked you to bring him a goblin-badge of Rank and an Insignia of Battle.\n6\tBring last set of components to Sterling Proudfoot\030Collect goblin-badge of rank\030Collect Insignia of Battle\tSterling Proudfoot is in Buckland, west of Bree and east of the Brandywine River. You should bring the last set of components to Sterling Proudfoot.\n",
[1385]="70000033\n1\tCollect Zorrgolug's matted hide\030Collect brimstone-tinged Tarkrîp-helmets (total: 5)\tZorrgolug prowls in Fasach-falroid in Angmar. Tarkrîp goblins dwell among the Orc-camps of Malenhad in Angmar. Fenton Marshley asked you to bring him the matted hide of the Warg Zorrgolug and brimstone-tinged Tarkrîp helmets.\n2\tBring the first set of components to Fenton Marshley\tFenton Marshley is at the Hunting Lodge east of Archet and north of Bree, in Bree-land. You have collected the first set of components Fenton Marshley asked you to bring him.\n3\tCollect glossy cave-claw skins (total: 10)\030Collect corroded Neekerbreeker-horns (total: 15)\tCave-claws and nerbeglir dwell in Angmar and other such evil places. Fenton Marshley asked you to bring him glossy cave-claw skins and corroded Neekerbreeker-horns.\n4\tBring second set of components to Fenton Marshley\030Collect glossy cave-claw skins (total: 10)\030Collect corroded Neekerbreeker-horns (total: 15)\tFenton Marshley is at the Hunting Lodge east of Archet and north of Bree, in Bree-land. You have collected the second set of components Fenton Marshley asked you to bring him.\n5\tCollect Rune of Winged Dominance\030Collect Insignia of Battle\tMormoz and Azgoth may be found at Carn Dûm in Angmar. Sorkrank and Burzfîl serve at Urugarth. Fenton asked you to bring him a Rune of Winged Dominance and an Insignia of Battle.\n6\tBring last set of components to Fenton Marshley\030Collect Rune of Winged Dominance\030Collect Insignia of Battle\tFenton Marshley is at the Hunting Lodge east of Archet and north of Bree, in Bree-land. You have collected the final set of components Fenton Marshley asked you to bring him.\n",
[1386]="700586CE\n1\tCollect Frostulf's tankard\030Collect Wildwood brigand boots (total: 10)\tHunward has asked you to bring him Wildwood brigand boots and Frostulf's tankard. Frostulf Splitknuckle can be challenged outside the western gate of Cotfast in the Wildwood.\n2\tDeliver the first batch of materials to Hunward at Trader's Wharf\tHunward is at Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood.\n3\tCollect mottled spider mandibles (total: 20)\030Collect bubbling droplets (total: 15)\tSpiders can found in Angmar and other dangerous places. Brimstone-leeches can be found in Malenhad in Angmar. Hunward asked you to bring him mottled spider-mandibles and bubbling droplets.\n4\tDeliver the second batch of materials to Hunward at Trader's Wharf\tHunward is at Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood.\n5\tCollect ashen Gorthorog-horn\030Collect goblin badge of rank\tTarlûg can be found at Carn Dûm in Angmar. Goblins can be found at Urugarth in Angmar. Hunward asked you to bring him an ashen Gorthorog-horn and a goblin-badge of rank.\n6\tDeliver the last batch of materials to Hunward at Trader's Wharf\tHunward is at Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood.\n",
[1387]="70002E98\n1\tCollect snow-encrusted Dourhand-boots (total: 10)\030Collect Grimgore's ashen hide\tGrimgore can be found in Fasach-larran in Angmar. The Dourhand dwarves may be found at Gabilazan in the Misty Mountains. Wáli asked you to bring him snow-encrusted Dourhand-boots and Grimgore's ashen hide.\n2\tBring first set of components to Wáli\tWáli is at the outpost of Noglond, south of Thorin's Hall and west of the dwarf-city of Gondamon. Wáli is waiting for you to return with the first set of components for which he asked.\n3\tCollect unyielding drake-scales (total: 25)\030Collect gem-encrusted nails (total: 15)\tDrakes and cave-claws may be found in Angmar and other dangerous places. Wáli asked you to bring him unyielding drake-scales and gem-encrusted nails.\n4\tBring second set of components to Wáli\030Collect unyielding drake-scales (total: 25)\030Collect gem-encrusted nails (total: 15)\tWáli is at the outpost of Noglond, south of Thorin's Hall and west of the dwarf-city of Gondamon. Wáli is waiting for you to return with the second set of components for which he asked.\n5\tCollect flawless scale of Lhugrien\030Collect Warg-keeper's token\tLhugrien and Athpukh may both be found at Urugarth in Angmar. Wáli asked you to return with a flawless scale of Lhugrien and a Warg-keeper's token.\n6\tBring final set of components to Wáli\030Collect flawless scale of Lhugrien\030Collect Warg-keeper's token\tWáli is at the outpost of Noglond, south of Thorin's Hall and west of the dwarf-city of Gondamon. Wáli is waiting for you to return with the last set of components for which he asked.\n",
[1388]="7000127A\n1\tCollect matted snowbeast-furs (total: 12)\030Collect brimstone-tinged Tarkrîp plates (total: 5)\tSnowbeasts can be found in the Misty Mountains. Goblins are encamped with the Tarkrîp Orcs in Malenhad in Angmar. Baillindiel asked you to bring her matted snowbeast-fur and brimstone-tinged Tarkrîp-plates.\n2\tBring first set of components to Baillindiel\tBaillindiel is at the Elf-harbour of Celondim, in Ered Luin. Baillindiel is waiting for you to return with the first set of components.\n3\tCollect clouded worm-eyes (total: 20)\030Collect revered wight-remains (total: 15)\tWorms can be found in Angmar. Wights can be found in Imlad Balchorth in Angmar. Baillindiel asked you to bring her clouded worm-eyes and revered wight-remains.\n4\tBring second set of components to Baillindiel\030Collect clouded worm-eyes (total: 20)\030Collect revered wight-remains (total: 15)\tBaillindiel is at the Elf-harbour of Celondim, in Ered Luin. Baillindiel is waiting for you to return with the second set of components.\n5\tCollect ashen Gorthorog-horn\030Collect goblin-badge of rank\tTarlûg can be found at Carn Dûm in Angmar. Goblins can be found at Urugarth in Angmar. Baillindiel asked you to bring her an ashen Gorthorog-horn and a goblin-badge of rank.\n6\tBring last set of components to Baillindiel\030Collect ashen Gorthorog-horn\030Collect goblin-badge of rank\tBaillindiel is at the Elf-harbour of Celondim, in Ered Luin. Baillindiel is waiting for you to return with the last set of components.\n",
[1389]="7006422D\n1\tCollect Torcadáll's spy-glass\030Collect hooked avanc-teeth (total: 18)\tAelindil has asked you to bring him a number of hooked avanc-teeth and Torcadáll's spy-glass. Torcadáll Wild-eye may be found in Thelgarth in the Angle of Mitheithel. Avanc can be found throughout the Angle of Mitheithel.\n2\tDeliver the first set of materials to Aelindil in Tornhad\tAelindil can be found at Tornhad in the Angle of Mitheithel.\n3\tCollect coiled spider spinnerets (total: 15)\030Collect unyielding drake scales (total: 15)\tSpiders can found in Angmar and other dangerous places. Drakes and other dragon-kind can be found in Angmar and Moria. Aelindil has asked you to bring him coiled spider spinnerets and unyielding drake scales.\n4\tDeliver the second set of materials to Aelindil in Tornhad\tAelindil can be found at Tornhad in the Angle of Mitheithel.\n5\tCollect a medallion of passage\030Collect an emblem of ritual\tUrro can be found at Carn Dûm in Angmar. Morthrâng can be found at Urugarth in Angmar. Aelindil has asked you to bring him a medallion of passage and an emblem of ritual.\n6\tDeliver the final set of materials to Aelindil in Tornhad\tAelindil can be found at Tornhad in the Angle of Mitheithel.\n",
[1390]="70000FAF\n1\tCollect Grimgore's matted fur\030Collect distasteful Corcur-emblems (total: 12)\tGrimgore roams Fasach-larran in Angmar. Corcur may be found near Helegrod in the Misty Mountains. Isdi has asked you to bring her Grimgore's matted fur and several distasteful Corcur-emblems.\n2\tBring first set of components to Isdi\tIsdi is at the ruins of Edhelion, near Thorin's Hall. Isdi is waiting for you to return with the first set of components.\n3\tCollect revered wight-remains (total: 15)\030Collect bubbling droplets (total: 15)\tWights may be found in Imlad Balchorth in Angmar. Brimstone-leeches may be found in Malenhad in Angmar. Isdi has asked you to bring her revered wight-remains and bubbling droplets.\n4\tBring second set of components to Isdi\030Collect revered wight-remains (total: 15)\030Collect bubbling droplets (total: 15)\tIsdi is at the ruins of Edhelion, near Thorin's Hall. Isdi is waiting for you to return with the second set of components.\n5\tCollect putrid slime of Helchgam\030Collect goblin-badge of rank\tHelchgam dwells in the pools below Carn Dûm in Angmar. Goblins guard the tower of Urugarth, also in Angmar. Isdi has asked you to bring her some putrid slime of Helchgam and a goblin-badge of rank.\n6\tBring last set of components to Isdi\030Collect putrid slime of Helchgam\030Collect goblin-badge of rank\tIsdi is at the ruins of Edhelion, near Thorin's Hall. Isdi is waiting for you to return with the last set of components.\n",
[1391]="70041399\n1\tCollect steam-scorched carapaces (total: 12)\030Collect Hogni's spiked helmet\tNorboglir can be found in the Eastern Malenhad in Angmar. Hogni Cleave-shank can be found at Gabilazan in the Misty Mountains. Sterkist says he'll need you to bring him norboglir-carapaces and Hogni Cleave-shank's spiked helmet.\n2\tReturn the items to Sterkist in Rivendell\tSterkist is at the Spire of Meeting, in Rivendell. You have collected a number of difficult-to-obtain items that your brother insists is required for the creation of a worthy piece of equipment.\n3\tCollect corroded Neekerbreeker-horns (total: 20)\030Collect grisly bat-talons (total: 20)\tNerbeglir can be found in the Eastern Malenhad in Angmar. Bats can be found in Angmar and other dangerous places. Sterkist says he needs corroded Neekerbreeker-horns and grisly bat-talons.\n4\tReturn the items to Sterkist in Rivendell\tSterkist is at the Spire of Meeting, in Rivendell. You have collected the second set of difficult-to-obtain components that your brother insists is required for the creation of a worthy piece of equipment.\n5\tFind Badge of Command and Putrid Slime of Helchgam and bring them to Sterkist in Rivendell\tHelchgam can be found beneath the evil city of Carn Dûm in Angmar. Lagmâs can be found at Urugarth in Angmar. Sterkist is at the Spire of Meeting, in Rivendell. Your brother asked you to find some more difficult components and bring them to him.\n",
[1392]="70002DB2\n1\tCollect Raillug's frozen hide\030Collect brimstone-tinged Tarkrîp-boots (total: 10)\tRaillug can be found in the north-western corner of the Misty Mountains. Tarkrîp goblins can be found among the Orc-camps of Malenhad in Angmar. Gwesgylliel asked you to bring her Raillug's frozen hide and brimstone-tinged Tarkrîp-boots.\n2\tBring first set of components to Gwesgylliel\tGwesgylliel is at Lin Giliath in Meluinen, in the North Downs. Gwesgylliel is waiting for you to return with the first set of components for which she asked.\n3\tCollect mottled spider-mandibles (total: 20)\030Collect bubbling droplets (total: 15)\tSpiders can be found in Angmar and other dangerous places. Brimstone-leeches can be found in Malenhad in Angmar. Gwesgylliel asked you to bring her mottled spider-mandibles and bubbling droplets.\n4\tBring second set of components to Gwesgylliel\030Collect mottled spider-mandibles (total: 20)\030Collect bubbling droplets (total: 15)\tGwesgylliel is at Lin Giliath in Meluinen, in the North Downs. Gwesgylliel is waiting for you to return with the second set of components she needs.\n5\tCollect blood-stained tally-stick\030Collect Insignia of Battle\tGríshakrum, Kughûrz, Dafrim, Sorkrank, and Burzfîl may all be found in Urugarth in Angmar. Gwesgylliel asked you to return with a blood-stained tally-stick and an Insignia of Battle.\n6\tBring last set of components to Gwesgylliel\030Collect blood-stained tally-stick\030Collect Insignia of Battle\tGwesgylliel is at Lin Giliath in Meluinen, in the North Downs. Gwesgylliel is waiting for you to return with the last set of components she needs.\n",
[1393]="70057F6E\n1\tObtain charcoal from the chef Ciriel\030Obtain clay from a potter\030Obtain flowers from the gardener Lebadar\tOn the Third Circle, Ciriel works at the ovens, and the potter next to the House of Craft. Lebadar may be on the Second Circle, at the base of the entryway to the Third Circle. Borlach has requested that you ask them for the following ingredients: charcoal, clay, and flowers, respectively.\n2\tReturn to Borlach with his ingredients\tBorlach waits for you on the Second Circle, near the entrance to the First Circle. You have gathered his ingredients and should let him create his paints.\n",
[1394]="700413BF\n1\tSpeak with Arvaethor\tArvaethor is near the pillaged lumber camp in Ringló Vale. You should speak with Arvaethor.\n2\tComplete Vale of Shadow\030Complete In Ethring's Defence\030Complete The Orkish Path\030Complete White Mountain Plague\030Complete Under the White Mountain\030Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated\tThis noble Arvaethor wishes to help you deal with the invasive White Mountain Orcs that descended upon Ringló Vale. You should complete a number of tasks in Ringló Vale, using the whistle to call your friend for help if you become separated.\n3\tTalk to Arvaethor to dismiss him\030Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated\t\n",
[1395]="70055079\n1\tDefeat dwarf-wights in Bâr Maenath (total: 6)\tBâr Maenath can be found in the western reaches of the Circle of Death. You have encountered dwarf-wights in Bâr Maenath and should defeat them.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many dwarf-wights in Bâr Maenath.\n",
[1396]="7003FF78\n1\tTalk to Mellien\tMellien can be found in Sardol, to the south-west of Alagrant in Blackroot Vale. Sarnir is concerned that the Dead's influence might extend to the south and has asked you to aid the people of Sardol.\n",
[1397]="70043405\n1\tTalk to Damrod\tDamrod can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath. Mablung has asked you to speak to Damrod about Faramir's daring attack that allowed many of their number to escape the city.\n2\tTalk to Mablung\tMablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath. You have spoken to Damrod about Faramir's gambit, and should now speak to Mablung about searching for Faramir in the tunnels under Osgiliath.\n",
[1398]="70043407\n1\tSearch for Faramir in the depths of Osgiliath\tFaramir might be found somewhere within the sunken labyrinth beneath Osgiliath. Mablung has asked you to search the depths of Osgiliath for Faramir, who may have fled into the tunnels in the wake of his attack on the fell-beast. You must complete the \"Sunken Labyrinth\" instance to complete this quest.\n2\tExamine the note at the abandoned camp-site\tThe letter can be found at the make-shift camp-site in the sunken labyrinth beneath Osgiliath. You have discovered a small, empty camp-site in the tunnels beneath Osgiliath. You should take the note and examine it before pressing onward.\n3\tSearch further in the depths of Osgiliath\tFaramir might be found somewhere within the sunken labyrinth beneath Osgiliath. You have not yet found Faramir in the tunnels beneath Osgiliath, but you should continue your search deeper in the labyrinth.\n4\tApproach the mysterious Ranger\tThe Ranger is standing near the gate to Muzgásh's chamber in the sunken labyrinth. You have defeated Muzgásh, but now a strange Ranger stands near the gate to his chambers. You should approach the Ranger and attempt to speak to him.\n5\tDeliver the note to Mablung and tell him of the mysterious Ranger\tMablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath. You have recovered a troubling letter and encountered a strange hooded Ranger in the sunken tunnels of Osgiliath. You should now return to Mablung.\n",
[1399]="70043406\n1\tSigns of the Ranger's passing can likely be found in southern Osgiliath, especially around the wharfs and nearby ruins. Mablung has asked you to pursue the mysterious Ranger you encountered in the sunken tunnels of Osgiliath. By the way he took to escape, Mablung suggest searching the wharfs and the nearby ruins.\t\n2\tReturn to Mablung and tell him of the Ranger's elusiveness\tMablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath. You have lost the trail of the mysterious Ranger, and should now report his elusiveness to Mablung.\n",
[1400]="70043409\n1\tPursue and confront the mysterious Ranger\tThe mysterious Ranger can be found somewhere within the ruined city of Osgiliath. Mablung has asked you to search the ruined city for any sign of the mysterious Ranger you encountered in the sunken tunnels. Note: You must complete \"The Ruined City\" instance to complete this quest.\n2\tReclaim Faramir's cloak from the fallen Ranger\tThe fallen Ranger can be found inside the Palace of Eldacar. You have defeated the corrupted Ranger bearing the cloak of Faramir and should now reclaim it for the Rangers of Ithilien.\n3\tDeliver the remains of Faramir's cloak to Mablung\tMablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath. You have defeated the corrupted Ranger that bore Faramir's cloak. You should now return the cloak to Mablung.\n",
[1401]="70043408\n1\tSearch the site where Faramir slew the fell-beast\tThe site where Faramir speared the great fell-beast can be found to the north-east of the Dome of Stars. In desperation, Mablung has asked you to search the site where Faramir speared a fell-beast in hopes of uncovering where he may have gone.\n2\tExamine Faramir's broken spear\tThe broken spear can be found near the ruined bridge to the north-east of the Dome of Stars. You have found the site as well as the broken spear that Faramir once wielded. You should examine the spear.\n3\tTalk to Mablung of the Nazgûl's captive\tMablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath. You have encountered one of the Nazgûl, the Black Blade of Lebennin, who claims to hold Faramir captive atop the Dome of Stars. You should tell Mablung of this at once.\n",
[1402]="7004340B\n1\tConfront and defeat the Black Blade of Lebennin\030Free Faramir from the Dome of Stars\tThe Black Blade of Lebennin and his captive can be found atop the Dome of Stars. Mablung has asked you to free Fararmir from the Black Blade of Lebennin and attempt to banish his spirit before the coming battle. Note: You must complete \"The Dome of Stars\" instance to complete this quest.\n2\tTalk to Mablung and tell him of Faramir's fate\tMablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath. You have triumphed over the Black Blade of Lebennin if only for a moment, and learned of Faramir's fate. You should return to Mablung with this news.\n",
[1403]="7004340A\n1\tTalk to Damrod\tDamrod can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath. Mablung has asked you to tell Damrod of Faramir's escape from Osgiliath.\n2\tTalk to Mablung\tMablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath. You have told Damrod of your successes in Osgiliath and should now speak to Mablung once more.\n",
[1404]="7003FFD3\n1\tRecover books (total: 4)\tThe books must be saved and preserved.\n",
[1405]="7006CE1E\n1\tDefeat Eshêgur the Reaper\tA fierce brute is guarding the way deeper into the mines of Ashunûg. Defeat Eshêgur the Reaper.\n2\tDefeat Anâkhi Ensemble\tA group of Anâkhi cultists stand at the passage even deeper to the mine, guarding something important. Their rituals must be stopped. Defeat the Anâkhi Ensemble.\n3\tDefeat Nâkhugir\tA monstrous scorpion dwells deep within the mine of Ashunûg. This must be the Anâkhi's idol, and it must be destroyed before it can bring terror to the nearby lands in Ambarûl. Defeat Nâkhugir.\n",
